<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ælfwynn</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 918</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ælfwynn was the daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aethelflaed">Æthelflæd, Lady of the Mercians</a>, and her husband Æthelred, and briefly ruled Mercia after her mother's death in June 918. In December of that year her uncle, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-the-elder">Edward the Elder</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wessex">Wessex</a>, removed her to Wessex and took direct control of Mercia, ending its separate rule. Nothing certain is known of her later life.</p></div>
